            The _Dickens Notes_ project allows users to explore the
            working notes Charles Dickens kept as he wrote his novels in monthly
            or weekly installments. In as few as 19 pages per novel, the notes
            are concise, dynamic records of Victorian serial composition. Access
            legible, visually faithful transcriptions of the working notes; read
            editorial annotations that interpret and explain the significance of
            the notes; learn about Dickens’s compositional practice; and
            consider how to incorporate _Dickens Notes_ into your teaching and
            research.
